      "text": "Given that Thanksgiving is on Thursday, November 23, we know that the day of the week for December 23 will be 31 days later. To solve the problem, we need to find out how many days are the difference between Thanksgiving and December 23. Since 31 days is an odd number, we have to look for the remainder when 31 is divided by 7 (which is how many days there are in a week). The remainder corresponds to the day of the week, or the number of days to skip to get to the desired date. In this case, the number of days to skip is 6 (31 mod 7 = 6). The remainder, 6, tells us that from Thursday, accounting for 6 days, we arrive at the 7th day of the week. The 7th day of the week is Monday. Therefore, December 23 falls on a Monday. Thus, the answer is \\boxed{Monday}.",
