      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the day of the week for December 23 given that Thanksgiving, which is on Thursday, November 23, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of days between November 23 and December 23.\n   - November has 30 days. Therefore, the number of days from November 23 to November 30 is \\(30 - 23 + 1 = 8\\) days.\n   - December has 31 days. Subtracting the days already accounted for (23 days) from the total number of days in December, we get \\(31 - 23 = 8\\) days.\n\n2. Add the 8 days from November to December to the 8 days from November to December:\n   \\[\n   8 (\\text{days from November to November 23}) + 8 (\\text{days from November 23}) + 8 (\\text{days from January to December 23}) = 8 + 8 + 8 = 24 \\text{ days}\n   \\]\n\n3. Determine if the total number of days is a multiple of 7. A week consists of 7 days, so we can find the remainder when 24 is divided by 7:\n   \\[\n   24 \\div 7 = 3 \\text{ remainder } 3\n   \\]\n   This means that 24 days is equivalent to 3 weeks and 3 days, because \\(24 = 3 \\times 7 + 3\\).\n\n4. Starting from Thursday and adding 3 days:\n   - Thursday + 1 day = Friday\n   - Friday + 1 day = Saturday\n   - Saturday + 1 day = Sunday\n\nThus, December 23 occurs on a Sunday. The final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Sunday}}\n\\]",
