      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine the day of the week for December 23, we need to calculate the number of days between Thanksgiving (November 23) and December 23 and then find the corresponding day of the week.\n\n1. Calculate the number of days between November 23 and December 23:\n   - November: 30 days, so 30 - 23 = 7 days.\n   - December: 31 - 23 = 8 days.\n   - Total days: 7 (Nov) + 8 (Dec) = 15 days.\n\n2. Determine the day of the week 15 days after Thanksgiving (four 3-day increments):\n   - Days of the week repeat every 7 days, so we find the remainder when 15 is divided by 7: 15 % 7 = 1.\n   - Adding the remainder to the starting day (Thanksgiving), which is Thursday, gives us Thursday + 1 = Friday.\n\nTherefore, December 23 occurs on a \\boxed{D}ay.\n\nTip: Remember that there is a 25th, a 26th, and a 27th on a leap year, and a 26th on a non-leap year. (\\(Leap Years:\\) a year which is divisible by 4, excluding decades ending in 00. (Non-Leap Years:\\) all other days.)",
