      "text": "To determine the day of the week for December 23, we need to count the number of days between November 23 and December 23. November has 30 days, and December only has 31 days. So, we are counting the days from November 23 to December 23, which are exactly 50 days.\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 50 is divided by 7 (since there are 7 days in a week). We can do this by calculating \\(50 \\mod 7\\):\n\\[50 \\div 7 = 7 \\text{ remainder } 1.\\]\nSo, the remainder is 1. This means that 50 days is equivalent to 1 day ahead of November 23 if we start counting from December 23.\n\nSince November 23 is a Thursday, adding 1 day to Thursday gives us a Friday:\n\\[ \\cancel{\\text{Thursday}} + 1 \\cancel{\\text{day}} = \\text{Friday}.\\]\n\nTherefore, December 23 is a \\(\\boxed{\\text{Friday}}\\).",
